# "A permanent you control" is control, not ownership (CR 110.2): Act of Treason steals Bot2's Ornithopter, so a This Town
# Ain't Big Enough aimed at it costs {1}{U} (CR 601.2f) - the pool is empty right after paying just two - and returns it
# to its owner's hand, Bot2's, not Bot1's (CR 400.3).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Act of Treason
This Town Ain't Big Enough
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Ornithopter
Forest x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Act of Treason.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {U}{U}
Bot1.Hand.This Town Ain't Big Enough.Cast
